@rekram1-node I've been playing with a couple of different approaches towards tackling this issue, but I'm currently undecided on which approach I should go with. Which reaction do you think would be preferable if a bad (syntax errors, other loading errors, or just plain missing) plugin is in the configuration line? 

1. Fatal error, refuse to start with an error message.
2. Nonfatal error, start but display a toast complaining about the bad plugin(s).

@coniferconcepts great idea, but can you please trim the duplicate parts of your issue?

Zed already does this for `.env` files: instead of reading them, the agent runs a `sed` command that replaces the secrets with `***`:

    sed '/^[^=]*=/s/^\([^=]*=\).*/\1***/' .env

